Shortly after, the next order came.
I have already made my first coffee today.
But this customer just wanted food.
He ordered a bun with cheese.
I took a warm sourdough bun from the basket.
Sourdough bread often has a hard crust.
But I have learned to cut the bread in half quickly.
Afterwards, I put a thick slice of cheese on the bun.
I arranged the food nicely on a small plate.
Now I had to deliver it to the customer.
There were many people standing in the middle of the café.
I balanced the plate and walked carefully forward.
I walked slowly past the other guests.
Fortunately, the customer was sitting right down in the corner.
He was waiting at the fourth table.
I placed the plate on the table in front of him.
"Here you go, a warm bun with cheese," I said.
"Thank you very much," the man replied.
It is lovely to see a satisfied guest.
